    "lawCode": "Rpld §101 sub 1 ¶(a) sub¶ (ii) cl (B), amd §101, ABC L",
    "lawSection": "Alcoholic Beverage Control Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S9013\n\nSPONSOR: COONEY\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the alcoholic beverage control law, in relation to\nlicensing restrictions for manufacturers and wholesalers of alcoholic\nbeverages on licensees who sell at retail for on-premises consumption;\nand to repeal certain provisions of such law relating thereto\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nTo make technical corrections and remedies of metes and bounds to\ncontinue the operation of a Black Button Distillery to maintain its\nability to hold a retail liquor license for on-premise consumption and\ncontinue the approval of an exemption on restrictions on manufacturers,\nwholesalers, and retailers from sharing an interest in a liquor license.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 removes the retailer metes and bounds from section 101.a of\nABC law and inserts language of metes and bounds for the wholesaler or\nmanufacturer.\n\nSection 2 inserts the retailer metes and bounds into section 101 of ABC\nlaw.\n\nSection 3 is the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis legislation seeks technical amendments to the ABC law based in\norder to align the metes and bounds Black Button Distillers in Roches-\nter, NY, to allow for the relocation and expansion of their manufactur-\ning, distribution and retail operations.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately, however, that section one of\nthis act shall take effect December 31 2024.\n",
